        explanation: `The derivative $Q'(t)$ represents a rate of change of $Q$ with respect to $t$, so its units are always (units of $Q$) per (units of $t$), namely ${item.qUnit} per ${item.tUnit}. Inverting the ratio, dropping the rate entirely, or squaring the time unit (which belongs to a second derivative) are the typical mistakes.`,
